    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0042" n="38" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg38"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.61/610: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-05-16T19:00:00+09:00">May 16, 1939—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 16—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>227. My British and French colleagues have recently told the Foreign Minister
                    under instructions that in the present negotiations with Soviet Russia<anchor
                        n="39" xml:id="d34-f1"/> their respective Governments have made no
                    commitments applying to the Far East but that if Japan now contracts a general
                    alliance with the totalitarian states their Governments may be obliged to
                    reconsider their position in this respect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d34-f1" n="39" xml:id="d34-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence on British and French negotiations with the Soviet Union, see
                        <ref target="frus1939v01">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>
                    </ref>, section entitled “Anglo-French-Soviet Negotiations …”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
